## 2. Procedure

`<skill>` means the directory containing this file. Scripts need only the Python 3.9+ standard library. Follow the steps in order and do not skip any.

1. Read the items of "3. Inputs" from the request. If an item marked "ask before start" is missing, ask the user all such questions now (CTL-03)
2. Run `python3 <skill>/scripts/run.py start --set <key>=<value> "<request text>"`. On exit code 3, ask the printed questions and rerun with the answers in `--set` (CTL-01)
3. TODO(skill-foundation): write the skill-specific steps as numbered lines, each containing a rule ID or a command in backticks. In the step that writes the output, point to the example to copy the form from (`assets/examples/<file>`). Add lines and renumber the following steps as needed
4. Run `python3 <skill>/scripts/run.py check`. For each finding, look up the rule ID in "4. Rules" and fix the output.
5. Write anything that could not be decided to `.skill-runs/{{name}}/notes.md` as "- " bullets, then run `python3 <skill>/scripts/run.py finish`. On exit code 1 go back to step 4. On exit code 0 reply with the printed text unchanged (RPT-01)

